-- title:
--   Closed translation- and smoothing-stable hull of a cusp form
-- statement:
--   Fix a homomorphism $\omega$ from the ideles $(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}})^{\times}$ to $\mathbb{C}^{\times}$, with $|\omega(z)|=1$ for all $z$, real numbers $a,b$, and a set $\Phi_0 \subseteq \mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}})$ which is a slab domain in the sense of `IsSlabDomain a b Φ₀`: $0<a<b$ and $\Phi_0$ is a fundamental domain for the image of $\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q})$ acting on $\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}})$ with respect to the adelic Haar measure of $\mathrm{GL}_3$ restricted to the slab $\{\,a \le \|\det\| \le b\,\}$ cut out by `ideleNormDetSlab a b`. Let $F : \mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}) \to \mathbb{C}$ be a cusp function for these data, i.e. $F$ lies in `automorphicSubmodule ω a b Φ₀` (left invariance under the global points $\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q})$, the transformation law $F(zg)=\omega(z)F(g)$ under adelic central scalars, and $L^2$-integrability for the measure `domainMeasure a b Φ₀`), is continuous, and is cuspidal along the two parabolic directions `IsCuspidalAlongP21` and `IsCuspidalAlongP12` for the pin data `productionPinsOf ℚ ∅ (fun _ => ⊥) (fun _ => 1) (AdelicBox.adelicBox ℚ)`. The assertion is that there exists a $\mathbb{C}$-submodule $V_0$ of $L^2(\mathrm{domainMeasure}\ a\ b\ \Phi_0)$ with the following five properties, where $[\,\cdot\,]$ denotes the $L^2$-class `toL2 ω a b Φ₀` of a member of the automorphic submodule. First, $V_0$ is its own cusp-generated closed hull: $V_0$ equals the topological closure of the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the classes $[f]$ of those elements $f$ of the automorphic submodule which are cusp functions and satisfy $[f] \in V_0$. Second, $[F] \in V_0$. Third, $V_0$ is stable under right translation on its cusp-function members: if $F'$ is a cusp function with $[F'] \in V_0$, $g \in \mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}})$, and the translate $x \mapsto F'(xg)$ is again a cusp function, then its class lies in $V_0$. Fourth, $V_0$ is likewise stable under smoothing: if $F'$ is a cusp function with $[F'] \in V_0$ and $\varphi$ is a smoothing kernel (a product of a smooth archimedean factor evaluated on the archimedean entries with the indicator of the elements whose component at each finite place $p$ lies in an open compact subgroup $K'_p$, equal to `localMaximalCompact3` for all but finitely many $p$), then whenever the convolution $x \mapsto \int \varphi(g) F'(xg)\,dg$ against adelic Haar measure is a cusp function, its class lies in $V_0$. Fifth, orthogonality to all translates transfers within $V_0$: for cusp functions $G$ with $[G] \in V_0$ and $F'$ arbitrary, if $\langle [x \mapsto F(xg)], [F'] \rangle = 0$ for every $g$ for which the translate of the fixed $F$ lies in the automorphic submodule, then $\langle [x \mapsto G(xg)], [F'] \rangle = 0$ for every $g$ for which the translate of $G$ lies in the automorphic submodule.
--
--   This produces the closed, right-translation- and smoothing-stable subspace of the cuspidal $L^2$ spectrum of $\mathrm{GL}_3$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ generated by a given cusp form, characterised by its properties rather than by a new definition; the final clause records that orthogonality to all right translates of the chosen form propagates to all cusp members of the subspace. It is used in the construction of non-vanishing inner products of translates for coset eigenfunctions, in [`LanglandsTunnell.CubicInduction.exists_inner_toL2_translateRight_ne_zero_of_isCosetEigenfunction`](thm.html#LanglandsTunnell.CubicInduction.exists_inner_toL2_translateRight_ne_zero_of_isCosetEigenfunction).
